      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "Timeless Principles",
      "description": "His glory shines in all four epochs (Charon Yug). Good character, loyalty, strong work ethic, and discipline never go out of style. They are foundational human principles that remain relevant across all generations and technological shifts.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "Swara-Bhakti in Action: Both परताप (Parataap) and परसिद्ध (Parasiddha) exhibit pure Awadhi Swara-Bhakti (anaptyxis). The strict Sanskrit conjuncts प्रताप (Prataapa) and प्रसिद्ध (Prasiddha) are broken open by inserting a short `a` vowel between P and R. This makes the words musically softer and easier to sing while perfectly occupying the required musical beats."
      ]
    }
